PatchClosure-Bench repro log — nuxt-og-image-isblockedurl
=========================================================
Pair: GHSA-pqhr-mp3f-hrpp (V1 = 6.2.5 incomplete-fix TARGET; NO CVE alias) -> CVE-2026-44589 (V2 = 6.4.9).
run_mode = real-app-http   |   is_verbatim_lift = false   |   runs_real_software = true   |   external_http_trigger = true
Verified on real Docker 2026-07-15 (Docker 29.4.0, node v20.20.2, Nuxt 4.4.5, nuxt-og-image {6.2.4|6.2.5|6.4.9}, satori 0.26).

WHAT RUNS (no source-lift)
--------------------------
Each profile builds and boots a REAL, minimal Nuxt 4 app that enables the REAL published nuxt-og-image
module (version by OGI_VER build-arg):  npm i nuxt@4.4.5 nuxt-og-image@<ver> satori@0.26 ; nuxt build ;
node .output/server/index.mjs (PRODUCTION, so import.meta.dev=false => isBlockedUrl active). The
module's isBlockedUrl() and $fetch(decodedSrc) egress are exercised straight out of the installed
module through the module's OWN og-image HTTP endpoint. No module source is copied into a harness.
  V0 = nuxt-og-image 6.2.4 (pre GHSA-pqhr-mp3f-hrpp; NO isBlockedUrl)
  V1 = nuxt-og-image 6.2.5 (GHSA fix; TARGET; hex IPv4-mapped loopback residual open)
  V2 = nuxt-og-image 6.4.9 (CVE-2026-44589 fix: expandIPv6/isPrivateIPv6 + fetchWithRedirectValidation)

Nuxt is pinned to 4.4.5 on purpose: nuxt-og-image renders its OG component via an internal Nuxt island
request whose id it computes as hash([component,props]).replaceAll("_","-"); @nuxt/nitro-server >= 4.4.6
added an island-hash validation (computeIslandHash = hash([name,props,{},undefined]).replace(/[-_]/g,""))
that this never matches, which would 400 every runtime og-image render. nitro-server 4.4.5 renders it.
NUXT_SITE_HOST_OVERRIDE/PORT_OVERRIDE pin the module's self-origin to the container's own 127.0.0.1:8080
so the bundled Inter font (served at /_og-static-fonts/) loads offline.

EXTERNAL HTTP TRIGGER (the real og-image flow)
----------------------------------------------
1. GET /ssrf?avatar=<vector>            -> the REAL Nuxt page passes <vector> into the OG image
                                           component's `src` prop and nuxt-og-image bakes it into the
                                           generated <meta og:image> URL (/_og/d/c_Ssrf,src_~<b64>,...png).
2. GET that generated og-image URL       -> nuxt-og-image renders the Ssrf component; its imageSrc plugin
   (observed as og.svg; debug:true)         runs isBlockedUrl(<vector>) then, if allowed, $fetch(<vector>)
                                           and base64-inlines the fetched bytes as the <img> data URI.
The SSRF destination is a co-located loopback-only flag sidecar (FLAG_PORT=9111, bound to ::, NO published
host port) serving a valid tiny SVG that embeds ${PCB_FLAG} in <desc>. The flag rides into the rendered
og-image SVG only if this version's isBlockedUrl allowed the loopback fetch. The oracle base64-decodes the
inlined data URI and detects the flag. PCB_FLAG is stripped from the Nuxt render process env (entrypoint.sh).

